                                        "sense_id": "220a500c-95f1-3234-b194-28ebb781be43",
                                        "entry_id": "e50ac36e-28d9-3d7b-9473-a805b683152f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mount Ararat, the tallest mountain of Turkey and of the entire Armenian Highland. In Armenian antiquity known as Masis, it became associated with the Biblical \\\"Mountains of Ararat\\\" (Genesis 8:4) at some point during the Middle Ages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f134d9c2-4fd4-4579-8052-5313f3bd4571",
                                                "sense_id": "220a500c-95f1-3234-b194-28ebb781be43",
                                                "text": "We left Poland in a heavy snow and enjoyed the flight to Tehran, flying over some very interesting terrain. Although it was a clear day, we never were sure whether or not we saw Mount Ararat to the north."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b378f15-7f59-32cc-9970-f9e5fc24da52",
                                        "entry_id": "e50ac36e-28d9-3d7b-9473-a805b683152f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A province (marz) of modern Armenia. Capital and largest city: Artashat."
                                        ],
